==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|sv}} {{term|þorp|lang=non}}, from {{proto|Germanic|þurpa-|lang=sv}}, whence also with German {{term|Dorf}} and Dutch {{term|dorp|lang=nl}}.

===Noun===
'''torp''' {{n}}

# (''before 16th century''): A solitary [[farm]], distant from other settlements
# (''16th century''): ''Officially defined'' as a very small farm
# (''17th century to early 20:th century''): A small farm, [[rent]]ed from a larger [[land owner]], where the rent was payed through work on the owner's land (''[[dagsverken]]'')
# (''after the 1940's''): A small [[cottage]] on the [[countryside]]

